 "notes": "Endpoints: the committed swagger (assets/swagger.json, /api/v1) is served by grpc-gateway generated code (pkg/apiclient/**/*.pb.gw.go) mounted with mux.Handle(\"/api/\", handler) — nothing the extractor could see (generated-server) until H2b's generated servers (2026-10-16): mux.Handle(\"GET\", pattern_X_0, h) with the path decoded from runtime.NewPattern; since then all 106 come out, and pkg/apiclient/ is in the endpoint scope. The hand-written net/http routes in server/ were added after reading the source (on 2026-10-16 also /auth/login, /auth/callback and /api/webhook from common.* constants; the last two are registered first by another app of the repo — the CLI's local login callback and the applicationset controller — and the route node keeps that evidence: multi-app-repo); mux.Handle(\"/api/\", gw) and mux.Handle(\"/\"+root+\"/\", StripPrefix(...)) are subtree mounts that come out as routes (mount-as-route), and registerDownloadHandlers(mux, base) builds paths from a string parameter (prefix-as-param). Calls: the React UI goes through ui/src/app/shared/services/requests.ts, whose get/post/put/delete prepend apiRoot() = /api/v1 — the paths come out without it (prefix-in-client-wrapper, H2-D12: the prefix is in the code). Calls written as requests\\n    .put(\"/x\") (receiver on the previous line) are not extracted at all (multiline-receiver). Expected calls = every requests.* call in five sampled service files. s.symlinksState.Get(key) is a cache lookup taken for an HTTP GET (non-http-verb). Since the v2 cheap fixes (2026-10-15): calls with the receiver on the line above are read, and like their siblings they lack the /api/v1 the requests wrapper prepends (prefix-in-client-wrapper); the subtree mounts and the cache Get are gone. Since F1.14 item 4 (2026-10-18): the UI's `requests` object (`export default { get(url) { return agent.get(`${apiRoot()}${url}`) } }`, with `apiRoot()` returning `toAbsURL('/api/v1')` and `toAbsURL(val)` returning `path.join(baseHRef, val)`) is read as a client wrapper, so `requests.get('/account')` is `GET /api/v1/account`: the 34 expected calls match and the 17 sampled calls re-judged at the source are right.",
